                                        "sense_id": "49ddbaac-e498-3607-8c4f-1fde0bafaa7d",
                                        "entry_id": "56f8f021-b422-3cbb-b6e2-fed375402c2f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to read and write; having literacy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "045edfe1-0d05-4cf1-9975-9b3266600f05",
                                                "sense_id": "49ddbaac-e498-3607-8c4f-1fde0bafaa7d",
                                                "text": "Intelligence tests are biased toward the literate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb694709-a770-4520-9c45-76e8c84b85be",
                                                "sense_id": "49ddbaac-e498-3607-8c4f-1fde0bafaa7d",
                                                "text": "Himachal Pradesh Chief Minister Sukhvinder Singh Sukhu on Monday (September 8, 2025) declared Himachal as a “fully literate State” on the occasion of International Literary Day. […] Journey from 7% to 99.30%: The Chief Minister said Himachal Pradesh had reached this goal well before the scheduled timeframe, adding that the journey from minimal literacy rate of around 7% to full literacy had been full of challenges, yet the State had consistently moved forward with the aim of providing quality education. […] Mr. Sukhu said the literacy rate in Himachal Pradesh had reached 99.30%, which is higher than the national benchmark of 95% […] Union Education Secretary Sanjay Kumar, in a video message, congratulated Himachal Pradesh on this achievement and emphasised the importance of providing skill-based education to the newly literate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17314666-3427-3ab5-b48e-cff7ab0e5459",
                                        "entry_id": "56f8f021-b422-3cbb-b6e2-fed375402c2f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Knowledgeable in literature, writing; literary; well-read."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9061cbc-a414-4350-b056-60f2b0e1554d",
                                                "sense_id": "17314666-3427-3ab5-b48e-cff7ab0e5459",
                                                "text": "The reason literature plays a unique role in any literate culture is its longevity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "507a2014-6eac-3f16-93a8-487f03087074",
                                        "entry_id": "56f8f021-b422-3cbb-b6e2-fed375402c2f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Which is used in writing (of a language or dialect)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa3aa108-9e6a-4edd-bf1f-01eaace24ed8",
                                                "sense_id": "507a2014-6eac-3f16-93a8-487f03087074",
                                                "text": "The Mongol emperor Kublai Khan even commissioned an alphabetic script for his empire, to be used officially for all its literate languages, Mongolian, Chinese, Turkic and Persian."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
